IMPORTANT SECURITY REQUIREMENT:

Never expose Gemini API keys, Firebase administrative credentials or other secrets in frontend source code.

Use server-side functions for AI requests requiring protected credentials.

If Firebase or other external services are not configured, provide a working demo mode using seeded data and local persistence where appropriate. Clearly distinguish demo mode from production mode.

Do not simulate successful cloud operations when no backend connection exists.

## 5. USER ROLES AND PERMISSIONS

Implement role-based access control.

### Platform Administrator

Can:
- Create and manage media organisations.
- Activate or suspend organisations.
- Create organisation administrators.
- View platform-level statistics.
- Manage system configurations.
- Manage subscription or licensing settings.
- View platform audit logs.
- Manage AI feature availability.

### Organisation Administrator

Can:
- Manage the organisation profile.
- Create and manage newsroom departments.
- Register users.
- Assign roles and permissions.
- Configure newsroom settings.
- View organisation-wide analytics.
- Manage storage and content policies.

### Editor-in-Chief

Can:
- View all newsroom submissions.
- Assign stories.
- Review submitted stories.
- Approve or reject articles.
- Request revisions.
- Schedule approved content.
- Manage the editorial calendar.
- Monitor journalist performance.

### Section Editor

Can:
- Manage assigned departments.
- Assign stories to journalists.
- Review submissions.
- Request corrections.
- Approve stories within authorised permissions.

### Journalist / Reporter

Can:
- View assigned stories.
- Submit story proposals.
- Write and edit articles.
- Upload interviews and supporting documents.
- Use AI assistance.
- Submit articles for editorial review.
- View feedback from editors.
- Track story progress.

### Producer / Multimedia Editor

Can:
- Upload audio and video.
- Manage multimedia assets.
- Transcribe interviews.
- Generate subtitles.
- Prepare multimedia content.
- Associate media files with stories.

### Viewer / Read-only User

Can:
- View authorised newsroom information.
- Access published internal reports.
- View permitted content without editing.

Enforce permissions in the backend, not merely by hiding frontend buttons.

