- Television report.
- Feature article.
- Interview.
- Investigative report.
- Opinion piece.
- Podcast.
- Multimedia story.

Story statuses:

- Proposed.
- Assigned.
- In Progress.
- Submitted.
- Under Review.
- Revision Required.
- Approved.
- Scheduled.
- Published.
- Archived.

Implement a complete workflow.

EDITOR CREATES STORY
→ ASSIGNS JOURNALIST
→ JOURNALIST WORKS ON STORY
→ JOURNALIST SUBMITS STORY
→ EDITOR REVIEWS STORY
→ EDITOR APPROVES OR REQUESTS REVISION
→ APPROVED STORY IS SCHEDULED
→ EDITOR OR AUTHORISED PUBLISHER MARKS STORY AS PUBLISHED.

The system must record the user, action and timestamp for every important workflow transition.

Include a Kanban board with columns representing story statuses.

Also provide a searchable and filterable table view.

